From 48ab4c05eb49d049d2c359bb808052e3cec7eefa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thomas Steiner <tomac@chromium.org>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 09:54:51 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] [iOS] Fix cut-off Gemma answers, and resume model
 downloads

Gemma stopped free-form answers after a few dozen tokens whenever the
conversation had constrained decoding enabled, which it always had.
Conversations now enable it only for turns with a response constraint,
and are reused only for turns of the same kind.

The Gemma download now survives interruptions, the app being killed
among them. Bytes go to a `.partial` file whose ETag and size are kept
next to it, and the next attempt asks for the rest with `Range` and
`If-Range`, starting over if the file changed on the server. Failed
attempts are retried with backoff, and the download checks for free
space first.

The minimal entitlements get extended virtual addressing back, which
PartitionAlloc needs to start, and the increased memory limit.
---
 .../app/resources/Chrome+Minimal.entitlements |   7 +-
 .../model/built_in_ai_engine.swift            | 254 ++++++++++++++++--
 2 files changed, 242 insertions(+), 19 deletions(-)

diff --git a/ios/chrome/app/resources/Chrome+Minimal.entitlements b/ios/chrome/app/resources/Chrome+Minimal.entitlements
index 7660f4099f124..649fa86c11d82 100644
--- a/ios/chrome/app/resources/Chrome+Minimal.entitlements
+++ b/ios/chrome/app/resources/Chrome+Minimal.entitlements
@@ -5,8 +5,11 @@
   Use of this source code is governed by a BSD-style license that can be
   found in the LICENSE file.
 
-  Used with ios_chrome_minimal_entitlements. The memory entitlements give the
-  on-device models of the built-in AI APIs room on devices with little RAM.
+  Used with ios_chrome_minimal_entitlements. PartitionAlloc cannot reserve its
+  pools without extended virtual addressing, and the on-device models of the
+  built-in AI APIs need the increased memory limit on devices with little RAM.
+  Enable both capabilities on the App ID in the developer portal; the App
+  Store Connect API cannot.
 -->
